      "created_at": "2017-07-31T00:23:59.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"morph147\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/839c29/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> morph147:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>i guess the question I have is how close is it to being a rip off of fate and what happens if it is?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Game mechanics and theme are basically not protected legally, so unless they ripped off some of the artwork the recourse is basically publically shaming. (I think this is good: I don't want courts to be in the business of judging when designs are too close to each other.) But, you know, they're currently running a Kickstarter, so public shaming could be quite effective. (If it is a ripoff, again, I haven't looked enough to decide.)</p>",
